            define_style: 4;
            style_name: string(STR_STYLE_COMBINED);
            style_lookahead_extra_aspects: 1; //See only 1 extra aspect (3-aspect signaling)
            style_combined_normal_shunt: 1;
            style_electric_enabled: 0x30;
            style_realistic_braking_only: 1;

            define_style: 5;
            style_name: string(STR_STYLE_LEVELCROSS);
            style_lookahead_extra_aspects: 0; //No extra aspects here, level crossings are slow
            style_electric_enabled: 0x31; //!!! look this up !!!

        }
    }
//}

/*
Explanations

extra_aspects                  
How many extra aspects (in addition to "stop" and "full speed") there are. Affects all signals in the game.  Is 2 here, for a maximum of 4-aspect signalling
Signals with fewer aspects display "full speed" for any excess aspect 

style_lookahead_extra_aspects  
Limit extra aspects available for specific signal types having less than 4 aspects
Limits what the train driver "sees", not what the game displays.  

Here: 1 for shunt, for they have 3 aspects [..]    [.·]    [: ] 
      1 for normal signals. 3 aspects (red/stop, single green/slow, dbl green/fullspeed)
      2 for distant signals, unlocking the fourth aspect that is "hidden" 
      unspecified (== extra_aspects == 2) for the 4-aspect signals
      0 for simple red/green or red/white 2-aspect signals      

style_no_aspect_increase
A series of such signals do not increase the aspect from one to the next. Which is how distant signals work – repeating without affecting the state of other signals. 

style_always_reserve_through
Trains will always reserve through, and never stop here. Necessary for distant signals.

style_lookahead_single_signal_only
Like style_lookahead_extra_aspects=0, AND lookahead stops at the next signal. Unclear what the last bit does. The train driver can only see "stop" or "full speed". Seems to have little effect when shunt signals don't have style_no_aspect_increase set?
